>> title: Classic Chocolate Chip Cookies
>> description: Soft and chewy chocolate chip cookies with a crispy edge
>> servings: 24
>> prep time: 15 minutes
>> cook time: 12 minutes
>> tags: dessert, cookies, chocolate
>> author: PantryButler

Preheat your #oven to 375°F (190°C).

In a large #mixing bowl, cream together @butter{1%cup} and @brown sugar{3/4%cup} and @white sugar{3/4%cup} until light and fluffy, about ~{3%minutes}.

Beat in @eggs{2} one at a time, then stir in @vanilla extract{2%tsp}.

In a separate bowl, whisk together @all-purpose flour{2 1/4%cups}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp}.

Gradually blend the dry ingredients into the butter mixture.

Fold in @chocolate chips{2%cups} and @chopped walnuts{1%cup}.

Drop rounded tablespoons of dough onto ungreased #baking sheets, spacing them about 2 inches apart.

Bake for ~{10-12%minutes} or until golden brown around the edges.

Cool on the baking sheet for ~{2%minutes} before transferring to a #wire rack to cool completely.
